# An almanac for the web: a menu, a table and a link, over the chapters of a book.
#
# The reckoning is done by the three chapters of the almanac book, which know
# nothing about pages. This program only sets their answers out: a menu to
# choose the year, and a table with a row for each feast.
#
# Run it in the playground and the page appears under what it says. Run from
# the command line, it sketches the page.

Use the page library.
Use the calendar, numerals and feasts chapters of the almanac book.

There is a heading called Banner whose wording is "An Almanack".

There is a panel called Desk.
There is a menu called Chooser whose hint is "Which year?" and whose panel is Desk.
There is a note called Verdict whose wording is "" and whose panel is Desk.

There is a table called Roster whose title is "The feasts of the year".
There is a row called Head whose table is Roster.
Now Head is leading.
There is a new cell whose wording is "Feast" and whose row is Head.
There is a new cell whose wording is "Date" and whose row is Head.
There is a new cell whose wording is "Falls on a" and whose row is Head.

There is a link called Source whose wording is "How the day of the week is worked out" and whose target is "https://github.com/monstercameron/EnglishScript/blob/main/examples/almanac/calendar.english".

# The years on offer, written as the Romans wrote them.
Let the offer be 2024.
Repeat 8 times:
  There is a new option whose wording is the roman of the offer and whose menu is Chooser.
  Add 1 to the offer.

# Set the table out afresh for a year: take away every row but the first, and
# write one for each feast.
To show a year (number):
  For each row:
    If the row is not leading:
      For each cell whose row is the row:
        Remove the cell.
      Remove the row.
  For each feast:
    Let the line be a new row whose table is Roster.
    There is a new cell whose wording is "{the feast}" and whose row is the line.
    There is a new cell whose wording is "{the feast's day} {the month title of the feast's month}" and whose row is the line.
    There is a new cell whose wording is the falling of the feast for the year and whose row is the line.
  If the leapness of the year is yes:
    Set Verdict's wording to "{the roman of the year} is a leap year of 366 days."
  Otherwise:
    Set Verdict's wording to "{the roman of the year} is a common year of 365 days."

# As the page opens, the year is 2027.
For each option whose wording is the roman of 2027:
  Now the option is picked.
Show 2027.

Whenever an option becomes picked:
  Show the reading of the option's wording.

For example, the number of rows is 8.
For example, the number of cells is 24.
